Well, you don't have to go ahead and sell your stuff to find out if it
makes up to 200g. Drop your stuff, write down how much the sk is
offering for each piece and answer "no" to the question of whether to
sell it. Add it up.

That said, unless you have unusually low charisma, your spellbooks
should certainly make up the difference. You can buy them back later.

You can avoid this in the future by dropping all your gold at your
feet before picking anything up. You get store credit, which lasts
between visits, and while you're standing on the gold, the leprechaun
shouldn't be able to steal it.  (He might steal it from between your
legs if your AC is poor, I think. But it won't affect your store
credit.)


